  [PASS] A8 (THE CLEANEST OBJECTS, AND THEY ARGUE FOR A MUCH SMALLER EFFECT) the ISOLATED Local Group dwarf spheroidals need no external-field prescription at all (x_e ~ 1e-4), and they sit BARELY above the framework's kernel -- a median far below the classical satellites and the M31 satellites.  Cetus and Tucana, the two best-observed of them, are essentially ON it.  So whatever the offset is, the objects where the prescription cannot be blamed show the LEAST of it, and that is evidence that part of the satellite offset is environmental or tidal rather than a property of pressure support   (Cetus +0.047, Tucana +0.117, Phoenix +0.383, Antlia B +0.231, UGC 4879 -0.091; isolated median +0.117 dex on N=5 against classical +0.492 and M31 +0.578)

